Windows Logon Types 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 10 and 11
1. What is a logon type?
Every successful logon (Event ID 4624) and failed logon (Event ID 4625) contains a Logon Type number. It tells the analyst how the account signed in: at the keyboard, over the network, through a service, by Remote Desktop, and so on. The same account name can look normal with one type and suspicious with another.
