4. How an analyst uses logon types
Always read Logon Type, Account Name, Workstation Name and Source Network Address together.
Compare with the baseline. A type 10 logon to a workstation that never uses RDP is unusual.
Failed logons (4625) with type 3 or 10 from external IPs are typical of internet-facing password guessing.
Match 4624 with 4634 using the Logon ID to see how long a session lasted.
Quick memory aid: 2 = at the keyboard, 3 = over the network, 4 = scheduled job, 5 = service, 7 = unlock, 10 = Remote Desktop, 11 = cached (offline).


